# `got := held.move() ?? fallback` hands the Option's payload to `got` and
# frees the box: the variable no longer holds it, so `got` shares no buffer
# with it. A lent payload left the box alive to the scope end, and the
# first write to each shared buffer copied it, which the 16 MB cap of the
# counting program allocator refuses for a 10 MB list. Every round's list is
# freed before the next is built (six rounds of 10 MB each fit), the None
# branch's fallback is the result, a closing payload closes once on each
# branch, and the checked heap stops at no bad free.
fixture: moved_carrier_hands_its_payload_to_the_fallback_result.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
env: JETPACK_ROOT={work}/jetpack
step: jet check main.jet
exit: 0
step: jet run -O0 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "batch: 6 of 6 rounds wrote in place\nlist: 6 of 6 rounds wrote in place\nnone: fallback 9 3\ntook 1\nfell back to 2\nclose 2\nclose 1\nheld at the end: 1250000\n"
step: jet run -O2 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "batch: 6 of 6 rounds wrote in place\nlist: 6 of 6 rounds wrote in place\nnone: fallback 9 3\ntook 1\nfell back to 2\nclose 2\nclose 1\nheld at the end: 1250000\n"
step: jet build --checked-alloc main.jet
exit: 0
step: {work}/.jet/build/main
exit: 0
stdout: = "batch: 6 of 6 rounds wrote in place\nlist: 6 of 6 rounds wrote in place\nnone: fallback 9 3\ntook 1\nfell back to 2\nclose 2\nclose 1\nheld at the end: 1250000\n"
